[size=5][b]Find The Needle — Multiplayer (co-op)[/b][/size]

Dig the same haystack with your friends. One yard, several players, everything
shared: the pile, the buildings, the money and the needles.

Connection runs over [b]Steam's relay network[/b], the same one official co-op
games use: [b]no port forwarding, no IP addresses, no VPN[/b]. You invite from
the Steam friends list and your friend lands in your yard.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Shared haystack[/b] — everyone digs the same pile and sees it change live.
[*][b]Shared building[/b] — structures, conveyors and platforms placed or
demolished by anyone show up for everyone.
[*][b]Shared economy[/b] — money, debt, hay sold, needles found and the whole
collection.
[*][b]Shared tech tree[/b] — an upgrade bought by one player unlocks for all.
[*][b]Shared needles[/b] — an uncovered needle is visible to everybody and can
only be handed in once.
[*][b]See each other[/b] — player figures with Steam names and the tool in hand.
[*][b]Steam invites[/b] — overlay invites, friends-list joins, or accepting an
invite while the game is closed.
[*][b]Chat[/b] in game, and a resync key if anything ever drifts.
[*][b]Streamer safe[/b] — the panel never shows IPs, Steam IDs or lobby codes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Find The Needle Demo (free on Steam), build V26 or newer
[*]Windows 64-bit
[*]Every player needs the same mod version
[*]Launch the game from Steam (invites need the overlay)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Unzip the download.
[*]Copy the [b]mods[/b] folder next to [b]FindTheNeedle.exe[/b]
(Steam → right-click the game → Manage → Browse local files).
[*]Run [b]mods\multiplayer\INSTALL.bat[/b].
[*]Start the game from Steam — the main menu now has MULTIPLAYER.
[/list]
To remove it, run [b]UNINSTALL.bat[/b]: it puts the game back exactly as it was.

[b]After every game update, run INSTALL.bat again[/b] — Steam updates overwrite
the file that registers the mod.

[size=4][b]How to play[/b][/size]
[b]Host:[/b] MULTIPLAYER → CREATE GAME → INVITE FRIENDS, then start or load your
save as usual.
[b]Friends:[/b] accept the Steam invite. Nothing to type.

[b]Keys:[/b] F2 panel · Y chat · F8 resync

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Machines that feed themselves from the pile (piston rake, robotic arm,
drone, scanner) run only on the host; on clients they stand still. This is
deliberate — it stops hay and money being counted twice.
[*]Loose props (buckets, sacks, bales) are per-player.
[*]Machine settings (filters, switches) are not shared yet.
[*]Bought tools are per-player; money is shared.
[*]Only the host saves. Clients never touch their own saves.
[*]The online leaderboard is disabled while the mod is active.
[/list]

